- $2x^{2} - 5x - 3 = 0$: You changed the sign of both roots. The root $\dfrac{1}{2}$ gives the factor $(2x - 1)$ and the root $-3$ gives $(x + 3)$.
- $2x^{2} - 7x + 3 = 0$: The root $-3$ gives the factor $(x + 3)$, not $(x - 3)$.
